  "family": "Lauraceae",
  "memo": "This tree is known for its aromatic, glossy green leaves that are often used in cooking. It has a dense, bushy growth habit, making it an excellent choice for hedges or privacy screens. The small, yellowish flowers it produces in spring are subtle but add a touch of charm. Over time, it can develop into a small to medium-sized tree with an attractive, smooth gray bark. Its evergreen nature ensures year-round greenery, and it thrives in well-drained soils and sunny locations. This tree is also quite drought-tolerant once established, making it a suitable option for urban landscapes.",
